        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T162]
        derives_from [@plan.RuntimeV2.D1, @plan.RuntimeV2.V2, @plan.RuntimeV2.V3, @plan.Types.V5]
        description
            Source phase Epic: flow-state-e7p.12 (open in the retained Beads record), with
            direct children flow-state-e7p.12.1 through flow-state-e7p.12.24 (all closed).
            Child IDs and receipts are recorded in their owning Workflow Tasks below.
            Source phase flow-state-e7p.12 depended on flow-state-e7p.13 (closed) and
            flow-state-e7p.27 (open) at migration. The .13 administrative prerequisite was
            satisfied historically; these Beads edges are provenance, not Workflow blockers
            or proof. Workflow @task.Rewrite.T271 is the current Phase 3 validation blocker.

            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.12.1 (closed; task).
            Original title: B01 — Own actor identity, allocation, and passive lookup.
            Deliverable: Consolidate A01-A03 into one actor identity boundary: stable and local
            ActorRef identity, incarnation allocation, and passive exact lookup.
            Recorded owner paths (historical):
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/test/actor-admission.test.ts`.
            External source blockers: none recorded.
            Source Bead close receipt: B01 identity/registry boundary accepted after final
            repair; coder 01a08174-e11d-7c50-8a8b-db52bb742e39 and reviewer
            01a0818c-ba2b-79f2-b66d-c4fca1d027c2 independently PASS; required
            focused/type/static/lint/coverage/unused/diff receipts passed.
            This is a historical receipt; it does not assert that the current checkout passes
            its recorded checks.
        acceptance
            Expected: Stable keys are runtime-local and preserve exact ActorRef<M> branding.
            Incarnations increase monotonically, are never reused, and fail before
            exhaustion/wrap without partial allocation. Lookup is passive and returns the exact
            existing actor or canonical MissingActorRef without mutation. Every local creation
            request receives a fresh opaque identity and cannot accept a durable address,
            restoration, or child capability; the result feeds B03's one shared admission path.

