    T156
        title        Publish atomic actor cuts and settle acknowledgements
        status       done
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T155]
        derives_from [@plan.RuntimeV2.D2, @plan.RuntimeV2.V4, @plan.Verification.V2]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.12.6 (closed; task).
            Original title: B06 — Publish atomic actor cuts and settle acknowledgements.
            Deliverable: Consolidate M08-M10 into one atomic commit, passive projection,
            publication, and private acknowledgement boundary.
            Recorded owner paths (historical):
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/turn-plan.ts`,
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/actor-engine.ts`,
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/test/turn-plan.test.ts`,
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/test/actor-engine.test.ts`.
            External source blockers: none recorded.
            Source Bead close receipt: Completed after B06 coder
            01a082a7-fa95-75d1-8e44-dedfe7e36b2e issue-only planner/engine seam and independent
            reviewer 01a082cf-99e6-7413-adc1-16f90bf23656 PASS.
            This is a historical receipt; it does not assert that the current checkout passes
            its recorded checks.
        acceptance
            Expected: A fully validated plan and typed P02 store result publish one immutable
            actor/store cut; observers never see a half cut. Machine, publication, and
            observed-store revisions advance only by their distinct laws, with fail-before-wrap
            and no partial publication. Validation and stale no-ops change no revision. A
            contained typed failure or defect before commit publishes exactly one issue-only cut
            with publicationRevision +1 and unchanged machine/store revisions; mixed Cause
            classification is defect > typed failure > interruption-only. A post-commit
            invariant failure preserves committed truth. Timer, completion, stream, context, and
            store projection facts publish without fabricated events, transition/action work, or
            machine-revision advance; lifecycle, terminal, cancellation, stream-terminal, and
            mapped-event facts never coalesce in this projection owner. Every accepted command
            settles exactly once: no-op without publication, contained issue after its
            issue-only publication, normal acknowledgement only after publication and evidence
            acceptance but before user-work settlement, and shutdown settles the current plus
            buffered accepted prefix.

    T157
        title        Own context baselines, waves, selection, and passive observation
        status       done
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T153, @T156]
        derives_from [@plan.RuntimeV2.V5, @plan.Verification.V2]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.12.7 (closed; task).
            Original title: B07 — Own context baselines, waves, selection, and passive
            observation.
            Deliverable: Consolidate C01-C05 into one context engine that installs the admission
            baseline, derives bounded provider-first waves, coalesces consumer turns, applies
            exact equality/defect laws, and keeps observation passive.
            Recorded owner paths (historical):
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/test/context-wave.test.ts`.
            External source blockers: none recorded.
            Source Bead close receipt: B07 accepted after repair pass 1; independent contract
            reviewer PASS.
            This is a historical receipt; it does not assert that the current checkout passes
            its recorded checks.
        acceptance
            Expected: Admission installs one immutable provider-first baseline and fixed binding
            set before the first active snapshot. Trusted forward/reverse topology yields a
            deterministic bounded provider-first wave. One provider publication causes at most
            one combined turn per dirty consumer after upstream providers settle, with no
            intermediate cut. Selection preserves authored null, undefined, function identity,
            scalar Object.is, and fixed named-record field semantics; unchanged selection
            suppresses work. A selector defect retains last-valid truth and emits exactly one
            issue-only consumer publication with publicationRevision +1 and no machine-turn
            revision, then retries only on a newer provider revision vector. Passive observer
            defects publish nothing. Observers atomically replace tracked dependencies without
            acquiring, refreshing, cancelling, invalidating, clearing, or mutating runtime
            state.

    T158
        title        Own actor lifetime and suspension truth
        status       done
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T154]
