        acceptance
            Expected: Only prepared→active↔suspended→disposed transitions are accepted; invalid
            moves fail, lifecycle publications never masquerade as machine turns, and
            actor:restore is evidence-only prepared→prepared. Every fiber, timer, listener,
            resource, and work item has one reachable actor Scope owner with
            cancellation/fencing registered before synchronous completion can escape. Suspension
            closes admission at one point, drains the pre-close FIFO prefix, cancels finite
            work, detaches live resources, and retains exact graph, cursor, generation, timer,
            and resumable truth without replay. Suspended publication occurs only after
            successful cleanup leaves zero live resources; cleanup failure keeps the actor
            suspended and blocks resume.

    T159
        title        Complete cleanup, resume, lease disposal, and runtime disposal
        status       done
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T158, @T157]
        derives_from [@plan.RuntimeV2.D2, @plan.RuntimeV2.V5, @plan.RuntimeV2.V6, @plan.Verification.V2]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.12.9 (closed; task).
            Original title: B09 — Complete cleanup, resume, lease disposal, and runtime
            disposal.
            Deliverable: Consolidate A09-A10 and L04-L06 into one terminal lifecycle boundary
            for cleanup, resume, individual owner-lease disposal, and whole-runtime disposal.
            Recorded owner paths (historical):
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/actor-admission.ts`,
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/lifecycle.ts`,
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/test/actor-admission.test.ts`,
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/test/lifecycle.test.ts`.
            External source blockers: none recorded.
            Source Bead close receipt: Completed after bounded repair and same-reviewer PASS.
            This is a historical receipt; it does not assert that the current checkout passes
            its recorded checks.
        acceptance
            Expected: Finalizers execute once in reverse acquisition/dependency order with
            consumers before providers; all primary and cleanup Exit/Cause lanes remain
            available, and cleanup failure blocks resume without rewriting committed state.
            Resume waits successful cleanup, revalidates retained providers, reacquires
            continuing work, preserves absolute startedAt/dueAt under Clock/TestClock, fences
            stale timer generations, and emits at most one overdue refresh without replaying
            finite work or input. Changed provider truth produces at most one serialized
            reconciliation wave; equal provider values stay silent. Only the owner lease may
            dispose one actor; dependent-disposal preflight rejects with deterministic exact
            refs and binding keys while preserving all state. Repeated disposal joins one
            terminal; successful cleanup tombstones once, while post-start cleanup failure
            remains untombstoned. Whole-runtime disposal subsumes leases, fences stale
            completions, drains the accepted prefix, and cleans provider-last exactly once.

