    T173
        title        Add production restore-admission validation seam
        status       done
        priority     high
        derives_from [@plan.RuntimeV2.V3, @plan.Verification.V2]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.12.23 (closed; task).
            Original title: Add production restore-admission validation seam.
            Deliverable: Provide the production owner seam required to validate restore payloads
            during actor admission. The runtime currently treats input as opaque and hardcodes
            every stable reservation as fresh-stable, so the proof case for rejecting restore
            data on a non-persisted actor cannot exercise a real contract boundary.
            No editable owner paths were recorded in the source Bead.
            External source blockers: none recorded.
            Source Bead close receipt: Completed: production restore-admission seam
            distinguishes fresh versus restored construction, rejects restore for non-persisted
            refs before reservation with typed SchemaValidation, preserves exact prepared
            snapshot/identity semantics, and passes actor-admission/runtime integration proofs.
            This is a historical receipt; it does not assert that the current checkout passes
            its recorded checks.
        acceptance
            Expected: A production-owned restore-admission path distinguishes fresh-stable from
            restored-stable; a concrete restore payload for a non-persisted actor is rejected
            with a deterministic typed diagnostic and no registry, lease, lifecycle, mailbox, or
            snapshot mutation; persisted restore uses the exact machine identity and prepared
            snapshot; actor-admission and runtime integration proofs exercise both lanes through
            runtimeSetup/assembly; focused rewrite types, static harness, runtime tests,
            coverage, unused report, formatting, and diff checks pass; independent same-snapshot
            review passes.

